1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,090
Okay, okay — new idea. Hear me out. Um…
no, wait. This one's actually big.

2
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:08,380
So… did we make it?

3
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:09,610
Read it.

4
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:12,130
It's blank.

5
00:00:12,170 --> 00:00:16,425
We don't write things down. We talk. Voice
notes, all day, every idea.

6
00:00:16,465 --> 00:00:18,410
What happened to that guy?

7
00:00:18,510 --> 00:00:20,430
I don't know how it ends yet.

8
00:00:20,470 --> 00:00:22,130
Then don't write it. Say it.

9
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:25,610
Okay. Did we build anything?

10
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:26,790
Three things.

11
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:27,880
Three companies?

12
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:29,960
Three products. Calm down.

13
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:30,920
First one?

14
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:36,390
Friends were throwing around a hackathon
idea. I shipped it in four, five hours.

15
00:00:36,430 --> 00:00:37,460
Five hours?!

16
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:42,720
Two, three days later I'd bought a domain
— didn't even know how domains worked.

17
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:46,010
Ten emails. One reply.

18
00:00:46,050 --> 00:00:47,130
One reply!

19
00:00:47,170 --> 00:00:52,810
Wrong customers. Small sites didn't feel
the pain. Big ones already had someone.

20
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:53,610
Second?

21
00:00:53,650 --> 00:00:57,980
Spending limits for AI apps. Nobody cared
about the bill yet.

22
00:00:58,020 --> 00:00:58,700
Third?

23
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:04,000
Safety rules for AI agents. Five months.
Best thing I've ever built.

24
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:05,780
You sleep at twelve, right?

25
00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:06,520
…Yeah?

26
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:10,760
I was up till three. Every night. Code,
customers, emails.

27
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:12,050
So who's using it?

28
00:01:12,090 --> 00:01:15,700
Fifty emails. Zero replies.

29
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:16,960
Did you try—

30
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:22,870
Reddit. One post blew up in a few hours.
Mods took it down. Account too new.

31
00:01:22,910 --> 00:01:24,400
…Of course they did.

32
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:25,990
Money?

33
00:01:26,030 --> 00:01:27,260
Zero.

34
00:01:28,510 --> 00:01:32,970
I'd promised myself five thousand dollars
a month. By December.

35
00:01:33,010 --> 00:01:38,285
Placements are next July. Half of me is
preparing for that. Half of me is here.

36
00:01:38,325 --> 00:01:39,460
Never all in.

37
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:42,560
So two months ago, I stopped. Everything.

38
00:01:43,610 --> 00:01:46,830
Was I wrong? To want it that big?

39
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:53,820
No. You're the only reason I started. You
just didn't know how long the middle is.

40
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:58,916
I kept asking AI for ideas. But real
problems don't come from prompts.

41
00:01:58,956 --> 00:02:04,240
They come from people. And I've been doing
it all alone, in one room.

42
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:05,360
So what's next?

43
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:09,240
Get out of this room. Talk to people.
Maybe physical AI.

44
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:11,500
Honestly, I don't know yet.

45
00:02:11,550 --> 00:02:12,550
It's okay.

46
00:02:12,590 --> 00:02:13,400
…What?

47
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:14,850
It's okay. You'll do it.

48
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:16,220
How do you know?

49
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:17,920
You're still talking to me.

50
00:02:19,970 --> 00:02:22,530
Don't write it. Say it.

51
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:25,990
Okay. New idea. Hear me out.
